[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Lines 23, 256, and 382: the class attribute tier is assigned the class SystemTier (a type) rather than a LifecycleTier instance or string. When register_singleton extracts declared_tier via getattr and passes it to _resolve_tier, the function receives a type which fails isinstance(val, LifecycleTier) and raises TypeError('Expected LifecycleTier or str, got type'). This causes every test setUp to fail during __initialize__ because the lifecycle registry cannot resolve the declared tier of DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner. The low-level contract low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi declares all three as @singleton_type('system') inheriting Singleton[SystemTier], and the support/lib/lifecycle.py _resolve_tier function requires a LifecycleTier instance or str, not a class type. The author's CHANGE header states this is the initial implementation with no prior fix attempt.
