[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Removed unreachable defensive code: (1) Eliminated redundant _upstream/_downstream pre-initialization checks in add_edge since add_node always initializes these dicts. (2) Simplified remove_node to use direct dict access instead of .get(_, set()) since nodes are always initialized. (3) Removed redundant cycle detection at end of topological_sort since validate() called at line 181 already raises CycleError for any cycle.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Added 6 new tests covering missing specification requirements: (1) compute_critical_path on empty DAG returns ([], 0.0), (2) next_wave returns empty when nodes are blocked on unmet deps, (3) SKIP_DOWNSTREAM transitive BFS through A->B->C chain, (4) DAGRunner.run() with SKIP_DOWNSTREAM records SKIPPED nodes in report, (5) DAGRunner.run() with CONTINUE_ON_ERROR records SKIPPED nodes in report, (6) run loop early break when next_wave returns empty while scheduler not finished.
